cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reproducibility artifacts, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LearnFlow: A K12 Gamified Adaptive Learning Platform for Difficulty-Calibration Research"
abstract: >-
  LearnFlow is a K12 gamified adaptive-learning platform released primarily as a reproducible
  research artifact. Its methodological contribution is to treat learning difficulty as a
  measurable, calibratable, decision-theoretic and governable first-class quantity. The artifact
  accompanies empirical work on the commensurability of difficulty scales, external-validity
  testing of the 85% success-rate rule, ordered-action bandits with a formalised flow channel,
  formalisation and conflict arbitration of gamification interventions, and reliability boundaries
  of LLM-based difficulty annotation. Every headline count in the documentation is recomputed from
  source by scripts under learnflow-backend/scripts/, and the consistency check fails loudly when a
  documented number diverges from the code.
